{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1527568-everyone-s-favorite-dr-who-actor","id":1527568,"title":"Everyone's favorite Dr. Who actor?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-28T12:14:47-08:00","id":1527568,"title":"Everyone's favorite Dr. Who actor?","content":"Mine is Matt Smith as I enjoyed his quirky behavior and I hope that the older stuff is even better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T13:03:33-08:00","id":1527572,"title":"","content":"Definitely Capaldi for me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T14:56:45-08:00","id":1527576,"title":"","content":"Yeesh, there's a difficult one. Part of the problem is that the history of the Doctor as a character is so obvious more than the person on screen. Lots of great actors have had the part, but clearly undermined by behind-the-scenes problems that what we see on screen is just not what other roles have shown them capable of. A lot of Internet lists top with performances that are bolstered by some of the best show-runners and writers the show has ever had.<br /> <br /> If we're just looking at the final result, my rather uncontroversial pick would be Tom Baker. There's a lot besides him there (as the 4th the original run had really hit its stride and voice where the early ones were way more scattershot in what they wanted to do with the character), but his performance is basically what everyone else is trying to do with a balance of whimsy of the Doctor's desire to enjoy experiencing all of space and time, and the gravitas for the serious dramatic moments when that falls aside. There's a reason he had the role for seven years when most actors only last three or less.<br /> <br /> In what's probably a bit more opinionated take, here's my list of the actors that I think elevated what they were given (even if a lot of it was unfixable no matter how good of an actor), so these are ones that are definitely favored actors, even if their Doctors aren't the best:<br /> <br /> 1) Peter Capaldi<br /> 2) Jodie Whittaker<br /> 3) Patrick Troughton (though a special mention goes out to being hit the hardest by the lost episodes so a lot of his work never really got its due because there weren't reruns of it like many of the others).<br /> <br /> In a different take, I think David Tennant is the actor I really wish they had cast later. I think he and Matt Smith were cast fairly young in the hopes of being able to take the role for longer than more established actors (and actors that know how to stick up for themselves) like Eccelston and Capaldi, rather then repeat the rapid turn over of 5 through 9, and while I do understand why a lot of fans love their runs as the Doctor, I think it shows too much that they haven't had the range of parts many of the other actors had before taking over. While I appreciate Matt Smith's career since being the Doctor, Tennant is the one who's done a lot of work that I really wish he had under his belt before hand. Just imagine how much better his run would have been if he'd already done Broadchurch, Jessica Jones, Good Omens, and Inside Man before, and was that much better at tapping into the darker side of the Doctor.<br /> <br /> I'm also hoping that Ncuti Gatwa doesn't get hit with the triple no-win of being a minority actor, questionable show running team, and being cast on the young side for a character that needs so much range. He seems like a strong choice, but as I started with, great actors have had meh runs with the character thanks to things beyond their control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-29T13:02:14-08:00","id":1527605,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> I think it's starting to happen to the current actor for Dr. Who this season but I wish it had to do with age itself, but it sounds like it's more to do with his skin color &amp; possible sexual orientation more then anything else and how RTD has acted to responses on social media about the changes he made to the lore. If I go by what Eccelston said in the past about what happened on the set during his time as Dr. Who is that his biggest gripe was with Russel T Davies and his like are unpleasant folks.<br /> <br /> I'm going into this series as a newbie and just started watching Christopher run on the series yesterday and it's different then what Matt Smith did and like you said is that he was an experienced actor compared to his costars.<br /> <br /> Maybe Dr. Who has reached the end of it's creative run and should start thinking of ending the series for awhile as it's been on since 2005 and had a good run that was above average compared to other shows that have come and gone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 12-29-2023, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-30T05:22:17-08:00","id":1527624,"title":"","content":"As a kid (in America, California) I started with Tom Baker on PBS. It was a fantastic show, great Sci-Fi. I don't think I was throw for a loop or anything when Pertwee showed up. Sci-Fi shows often just did whatever and you rolled with it or moved on.<br /> <br /> I saw all but the first two doctors by the time Napster came along and then I eventually Downloaded all the original series and watched them in order.<br /> <br /> Colin Baker eventually grew on me. But not a Doctor anyone would have wished for if they knew how his run would turn out I would think. Strangely enough, Matt Smith took a little time to grew on me, maybe 3 arcs, but I love him as much as anyone there after.<br /> <br /> I've now seen all but Jodie due to access during her run. I <b>hear</b> she was bad, but I judge for myself when I can finally see her.<br /> <br /> Even saying X is my favorite, I could also put down a small margin of error and call it a 5 way tie. But really Patrick Trouten is my favorite. His care for his companions and the people he's out to save seem to be a bit above the others, but even then, it's hard not to call it a 13-14 way tie, ya know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24473-willowfang","name":"Willowfang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-30T10:49:46-08:00","id":1527631,"title":"","content":"I've heard the same thing about Jodi Whitaker from my friends who are longtime fans of the series, but I will reserve judgement myself when I get around to watching it. For all I know I might find myself liking her even if I don't like the scripts if there bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-30T10:55:15-08:00","id":1527633,"title":"","content":"On a related topic who is everybody's favorite companion for Dr. Who? So far I've only seen Amy Pond by Karen Gillian and I enjoyed her and so far Rose Tyler by Billi Piper seems enjoyable and is bringing out better elements of the 9th Doctor after dealing with the loss of his species. Do you have any recommendations of what other companions I should check out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-30T14:22:41-08:00","id":1527639,"title":"","content":"I have mixed feelings about the Jodie Whittaker Doctor, but she acted her damned heart out to make three years worth of compelling performances. But there's a reason she's on my list of actors that elevated their material...even if it wasn't always enough to make great material.<br /> <br /> This actually gets into a hard part about addressing the companions. There are two interconnected shifts between the original Doctor Who run and the revival run. The originals were more &quot;self-contained&quot; even if not to one episode. It wasn't Star Trek with lots of stand alone stories and a few multi-episodes here or there, or an episode that followed up on an older one. But most of the stories were given as many episodes as they needed, and then the show moved on. &quot;This story needs three episodes to work, this needs four, this needs one, boom we have a year's worth of stories lets get to it.&quot; This pushed the older shows to be much more from the Doctor's perspective and made the companions more ancillary. This isn't to say the old companions were bad or uncompelling, but they weren't the focus of the plots because the plots jumped around as the Doctor hopped into the Tardis and moved on to the next adventure.<br /> <br /> The revival shows shifted to having a bigger focus on &quot;building up&quot; to a big arc: A smattering of isolated plots would get sprinkled with hints and foreshadowing of things to come, and then usually a few episodes of climactic stuff. This also pushed the companions much more into the forefront of the stories because the stories moved to be much more how a companion would experience things. So the revival companions got way more focus in the plot, and way more character development, because there would be a more linear continuity to the episodes.<br /> <br /> Obviously there's some preference on this, and both approaches have their strengths and weaknesses. But it creates a very big gulf of what people think a companion is supposed to be, and therefore what makes for a good one.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think the most important thing to a companion is that they offer such a radically different perspective from the Doctor. That is even explicitly in the shows, part of why the Doctor does it: the Doctor can't think like a mortal linear-time-frame person and wants to experience and interrogate that perspective vicariously. This... probably unsurprisingly, puts me at odds with a lot of Doctor Who fans because the most popular companions tend to be the revival ones where they're far more relatable thanks to having more character development, and have far deeper ties to the Doctor. I agree that a lot of them a great and fun characters for it, but it gets away from the core dynamic; as well as letting the story play with varied numbers (and even species) of companions by getting too wrapped up in how one or two companions interact with the Doctor over a few years of shows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T01:45:40-08:00","id":1527686,"title":"","content":"Colin Baker is my favourite, but only his post-Evelyn Smythe version of the Doctor (which is where he mellows out somewhat). It's a shame that he was never allowed to do the planned character arc on-screen.<br /> <br /> The runners up are, of course, Paul McGann and Rowan Atkinson, with Troughton and Pertwee fighting for fourth place. I am still annoyed that McGann wasn't allowed to be in Day if the Doctor.<br /> <br /> My view on Jodie is 'glad I checked out after two episodes, looking forward to what Big Finish gives you'.<br /> <br /> <br /> As to companions, well clearly there is only one correct answer (assuming we're not counting Scream of the Shalka), and that is Katy Manning's Jo Grant. Her lack of scientific knowledge makes her the perfect Watson to the Doctor, but has a complimentary skillset that was suited to the stories of the UNIT era","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T07:53:25-08:00","id":1527692,"title":"","content":"Pertwee. I met him at a convention. I was just a little kid and was completely starstruck. I could barely say anything because I was meeting <i>the</i> Dr. Who. He signed an autographed picture for me. I guess I was so stunned I couldn't say anything and just kind of sat there with my mouth hanging open. He laughed and pulled out his wallet and gave me a Pound note. I remember he showed off the naval tattoos he had on his forearms and talked about how he needed to wear long sleeves on the show because, obviously, Dr. Who wouldn't have English naval tattoos. <br /> <br /> My favorite companion was always Leela from The 4th Dr's run. She was a warrior, and it was always great to see her pull out her knife and kill people with it, while The Doctor tried to hold her back from her more aggressive instincts. It was a really fun change from the more typical sci-fi dynamic, where female characters were often relegated to being helpless damsels. Instead she was functioning as the Doctor's bodyguard, and on occasion, hitman. I always really enjoyed her, thought she brought a fun change of pace to the show.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T11:51:35-08:00","id":1527942,"title":"","content":"So far I like Christopher Esscaliton and Matt Smith right now and just started with the David Tennent run and so far Rose Tyler from her time with the 9th Doctor is my favorite as she helped heal him from his trauma of wiping out his species in there war with the Daleks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T11:00:10-08:00","id":1528816,"title":"","content":"Well I'm starting to like the David Tennent run as the Doctor and I'm warming up to Martha Jones as a great replacement for Rose Tyler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-30T12:08:05-08:00","id":1529726,"title":"","content":"After watching David Tennent's run as the Doctor I can see why he is considered one of the most popular ones in the series, he might edge out Matt Smith slightly in my current list. I hope I will enjoy Peter Capadi's run as the Doctor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T09:11:15-07:00","id":1532943,"title":"","content":"I will bring back my long time complaints about Russel T Davies. The man is magnificent at writing characters and character interaction. He's pretty good at writing spectacle too. He's not good at writing science fiction. That's why he takes heavy inspiration from, and sometimes outright steals, from previous stories. Most of the episodes he's best known for. Dalek is inspired by Jubilee. Family of Blood is an adaptation of Human Nature. Etc. He also tends to be graceless when incorporating political elements into his stories. That's not a complaint about his politics, it's a complaint about his ability.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, I don't know that he's aware of his problems so I don't have much faith he can avoid them this time around. The four episodes last year were mostly good, but some of his problems were leaking through. The most worrying one is the quick and uncharitable descriptions of how the Moffat era companions left. It came across like RTD was hurt that people didn't like how he handled Donna's departure and was criticizing the fanbase for being hypocritical. It's rarely a good look criticizing the fanbase, and it makes it look like RTD doesn't understand what the complaint even was. Most importantly, though, this was a scene that could have played into his strengths and he didn't use it that way.<br /> <br /> I have hopes, though, that Davies main purpose here it to revitalize interest in the show while training up a new showrunner. He's good with spectacle and in the short term that's what the show needs.<br /> <br /> As far as Doctors go:<br /> <br /> Matt Smith and Sylvester McCoy are my favorite Doctors.<br /> Tom Baker and David Tennant are the most fun.<br /> Jodie Whittaker and Colin Baker were the outstanding Doctors brought down by terrible writing. Capaldi almost suffers the same fate.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T09:37:45-07:00","id":1532945,"title":"","content":"Oh, and I recently ran across rankings of the first and last episodes of each Doctor that I wrote right before Capaldi debuted. I won't post the entire articles, but I figured I'd give the rankings and add in 12 and 13. I need to think about how to handle 14 and 15 before I add them.<br /> <br /> First episodes are in ascending order:<br /> <br /> 14 - The Sixth Doctor - The Twin Dilemma<br /> 13 - The Seventh Doctor - Time and the Rani<br /> 12 - The Eighth Doctor - The Enemy Within<br /> 11 - The Fourth Doctor - Robot<br /> 10 - The Tenth Doctor - The Christmas Invasion<br /> 9 - The Fifth Doctor - Castrovalva<br /> 8 - The Alternate Ninth Doctor - Scream of the Shalka - It was canon while it was in production, not anymore.<br /> 7 - The Twelfth Doctor - Deep Breath<br /> 6 - The Thirteenth Doctor - The Woman Who Fell to Earth<br /> 5 - The First Doctor - An Unearthly Child<br /> 4 - The Third Doctor - Spearhead From Space<br /> 3 - The Ninth Doctor - Rose<br /> 2 - The Eleventh Doctor - The Eleventh Hour<br /> 1 - The Second Doctor - The Power of the Daleks<br /> <br /> Final episodes are in descending order<br /> <br /> 1 - The Fifth Doctor - Caves of the Androzani<br /> 2 - The Ninth Doctor - A Parting of Ways<br /> 3 - The Second Doctor - The War Games<br /> 4 - The Third Doctor - Planet of the Spiders<br /> 4.5 - What should have been the last Twelfth Doctor - The Doctor Falls<br /> 5 - The Fourth Doctor - Logopolis<br /> 5.5 - Alternate Seventh Doctor Ending - Death Comes to Time<br /> 5.5 - Alternate Sixth Doctor Ending - Spiral Scratch<br /> 6 - The First Doctor - The Tenth Planet<br /> 7 - The Eleventh Doctor - The Time of the Doctor<br /> 8 - The Eighth Doctor - The Night of the Doctor<br /> 9 - The Thirteenth Doctor - The Power of the Doctor<br /> 10 - The Seventh Doctor - The Enemy Within<br /> 11 - The Twelfth Doctor - Twice Upon a Time<br /> 13 - The Sixth Doctor - Time and the Rani<br /> 13 - The Tenth Doctor - The End of Time<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T17:51:57-07:00","id":1532974,"title":"","content":"So far my favorite Doctors are Christopher Ellecstion, David Tennent and Matt Smith and I'm going to check out the earlier actors after I watched the first season of Capadi's run where I wasn't impressed by as I think the writing suffered in the season and his Doctor wasn't as fun or as likeable as the other three.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T19:53:49-07:00","id":1532977,"title":"","content":"Capaldi hits his stride in his second season. The writing varies wildly though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-22T12:46:22-07:00","id":1533018,"title":"","content":"Just like the first season of Capaldi and I think I will give the rest of the series a pass and focus on some the older Doctors and see what they were like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}